# The QA gate itself is tracked; its 312MB of screenshots and its generated
# reports are not. CLAUDE.md makes qa-audit.js the check to run before calling
# website work done, and until now it lived on one laptop and nowhere else —
# which is why a fix to it (#1172, and the SITE_ROOT bug before it) could not be
# shared or reviewed. Re-including a path needs its directory un-ignored first,
# hence the three lines rather than one.
!_dev/qa/
_dev/qa/*
!_dev/qa/qa-audit.js
pages/
blog-backup/
qa-report.html
*.py


